{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.ChannelMeridianIdentification","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.ChannelMeridianIdentification","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Knot.FigureEightDeformedMeridianWinding","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.PhiBSArgumentIdentification"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ChannelMeridianIdentification.not_neg_of_theta_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ChannelMeridianIdentification.not_neg_of_theta_zero","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ChannelMeridianIdentification.lean#L184-L193","doc":"The falsification, stated as the impossibility it is: with `ϑ = 0` at both\nanchors, the second anchor cannot be negative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ChannelMeridianIdentification.no_sign_flip_of_theta_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ChannelMeridianIdentification.no_sign_flip_of_theta_zero","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ChannelMeridianIdentification.lean#L166-L182","doc":"**No sign flip at vanishing angular deformation.**  In the T5 shape\n`S = A_ω · κ · (ln²q₀ − ϑ²)`, two anchors that both have `ϑ = 0` carry `S` of\nthe SAME (positive) sign, whatever their Stokes constants.\n\nThis is what refutes the identification against data: the two anchors are\nMEASURED with `S_μ > 0 > S_p`, and §3 forces `ϑ = 0` at the boost-dominated one\nwhile §2 forces the same degenerate colour at both. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ChannelMeridianIdentification.color_one_and_theta_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ChannelMeridianIdentification.color_one_and_theta_zero","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ChannelMeridianIdentification.lean#L152-L162","doc":"**The identification collapses a boost-dominated anchor to `ϑ = 0`.**\nCombining §2 and §3: the colour is degenerate AND the angular deformation\nvanishes identically. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ChannelMeridianIdentification.winding_eq_zero_of_boost_dominated","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ChannelMeridianIdentification.winding_eq_zero_of_boost_dominated","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ChannelMeridianIdentification.lean#L129-L150","doc":"**Boost dominance kills the winding.**  The meridian's imaginary part is\n`−2πk`, so `Im²u = 4π²k²`.  If the anchor is boost-dominated — `ϑ² < t²`, the\n`S > 0` branch of `s_channel_sign_pos` — and the substrate scale is subarchimedean\nin the sense `|t| < 2π` (amply true at `t = ln q₀ ≈ 0.104`), then `k = 0`.\n\nThere is no room here: the smallest nonzero winding already contributes\n`2π ≈ 6.28`, some sixty times `ln q₀`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ChannelMeridianIdentification.re_ne_log_of_color_ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ChannelMeridianIdentification.re_ne_log_of_color_ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ChannelMeridianIdentification.lean#L120-L125","doc":"Contrapositive, in the form the deformed volume conjecture cares about: at\nany non-degenerate colour `N ≠ 1`, the substrate-matched meridian's real part is\nNOT `ln q₀`, so the T5 hypothesis `hRe` fails outright. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ChannelMeridianIdentification.color_eq_one_of_re_eq_log","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ChannelMeridianIdentification.color_eq_one_of_re_eq_log","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ChannelMeridianIdentification.lean#L98-L118","doc":"**`Re u = ln q₀` forces trivial colour.**  The substrate-matched meridian\nhas real part `N·t`; demanding it equal `t` (the T5 hypothesis `hRe`, with\n`t = ln q₀ ≠ 0` for `q₀ ≠ 1`) forces `N = 1`.\n\nThis is the quantitative form of the identification's cost: `hRe` is not a free\nnormalisation, it pins the colour to the one value at which the coloured Jones\npolynomial is trivial.\n\nTechnically easy (`aesop` discharges it); its weight is in what it says, not in\nits proof.  It is nonetheless falsifiable — without `ht` it is false at\n`N = 5, t = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ChannelMeridianIdentification.channelFree_u","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ChannelMeridianIdentification.channelFree_u","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ChannelMeridianIdentification.lean#L93-L94","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ChannelMeridianIdentification.channelFree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ChannelMeridianIdentification.channelFree","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ChannelMeridianIdentification.lean#L72-L91","doc":"**The channel is conservative over `u` (branch (a), proved).**  For an\narbitrary deformation map `u`, an arbitrary deformed volume `V` and an arbitrary\nStokes constant `A`, the S-channel class is inhabited — witnessed by the `S`\nthat the class identity itself names.  Hence `SDeformedVolumeChannel` places NO\ncondition whatsoever on `u`, and in particular does not impose the Murakami\nsubstrate matching `u = N·t − 2πi·k`.  Any quantization of `Im u` must therefore\ncome from OUTSIDE the class.\n\n**This is deliberately a `def`, never an `instance`.**  Registering it for\ntypeclass resolution would let every `[SDeformedVolumeChannel S]` theorem\ndischarge itself against a tautologically-defined `S` and silently trivialise\nthe downstream chain.  It also does NOT fabricate the open conjecture: the\nconjecture concerns the MEASURED `S_K`, whereas the `S` built here is defined to\nsatisfy the identity. ","signatureChunk":0}]}